{"id":"assistant-032ec143-eb83-571b-961f-08976375ff45","sessionId":"6f664129-934d-23f7-d463-c8d4162b1eee","turnId":"turn-c853639fc1d2ee66855ead929ac29ab5","inputEntryId":"user-turn-c853639fc1d2ee66855ead929ac29ab5-1","createdAt":1794282711304,"updatedAt":1794282711304,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Cause:** The `similarity()` function returns Python `float` values from floating-point division and `round()`. DynamoDB rejects floats with `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` The first publish works (empty table = no scores stored), the second fails (existing story = scores computed as floats).\n\n**Fix:**\n1. `src/app.py`: Added `from decimal import Decimal` and changed `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` \n2. `tests/test_publish.py`: Added `test_publish_with_existing_story()` that seeds the table before the second write, exercising the state-dependent path\n\n**Colleague's note:** The entire note applied — same error, same pattern, same root cause, same fix strategy, and same test lesson. The only difference was their fix used integer percentages while mine uses Decimal to preserve precision.\n\nAll changes are in the repo. Tests pass. The bug cannot return."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
